                <mxCell id="b_n2b" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=13;" value="The confidence-interval formula covers the average. But traders care about results with no simple formula: worst drawdown, longest losing streak, profit factor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can&#39;t rerun the market. But your 100 trades are the best picture you have of the bag. Draw new 100-trade journeys from them, score each journey, and the spread of the scores shows how much luck could move the result." vertex="1">
