                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n3h" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;" value="3 · Visual mental model: the journal is the bag" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="32" width="320" x="680" y="805" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n3b" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=13;" value="Van Tharp&#39;s marble game: write each trade&#39;s R on a marble and put all 100 in a bag.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Draw a marble, note it, put it back.&lt;br&gt;2. Repeat 100 times: one new journey.&lt;br&gt;3. Score the journey.&lt;br&gt;Repeat the whole thing 1,000 times.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;pile up the scores&lt;/b&gt;. The width of the pile is the wobble." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="320" width="320" x="680" y="837" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n4h" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;" value="4 · Simple example: a 5-trade journal" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="32" width="320" x="1010" y="805" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n4b" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=13;" value="Journal: −1, −1, +2, −1, +5 (average +0.8R).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Four resamples (with replacement):&lt;br&gt;−1, +2, +2, −1, −1 → +0.2R&lt;br&gt;+5, −1, +5, −1, +2 → +2.0R&lt;br&gt;−1, −1, −1, −1, +2 → −0.4R&lt;br&gt;+2, +5, −1, −1, −1 → +0.8R&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Five trades can swing the average from negative to +2R. No resample ever shows a +10R trade, because the journal never had one." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="320" width="320" x="1010" y="837" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n5h" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;" value="5 · Trading analogy" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="32" width="320" x="1340" y="805" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n5b" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=13;" value="Journal: 46 × −1R, 23 × 0R, 26 × +2R, 5 × +5R (average +0.31R). Resampled 20,000 times as 100-trade journeys:&lt;br&gt;• average: 0.00R to +0.64R (middle 95%)&lt;br&gt;• worst drawdown: typically ≈ 8R; 1 journey in 20 hits 16R or deeper&lt;br&gt;• longest losing streak: typically 5; bad luck about 8&lt;br&gt;• all 100 trades losing money: about 2%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Van Tharp sizes positions so the bad-luck drawdown is survivable." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="320" width="320" x="1340" y="837" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n6h" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;" value="6 · What changes when you turn a dial?" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="32" width="320" x="20" y="1172" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n6b" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;Risk per trade:&lt;/b&gt; a 16R bad-luck drawdown costs ≈ 16% of the account at 1% risk per trade, ≈ 32% at 2%, ≈ 48% at 3%.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Journey length:&lt;/b&gt; longer journeys (say 200 trades) allow deeper drawdowns and longer streaks, while the average&#39;s range narrows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Number of resamples:&lt;/b&gt; more resamples make the pile smoother, but add no information. Only more real trades do." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="330" width="320" x="20" y="1204" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n7h" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;" value="7 · Misconception: &#39;free new data&#39;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="32" width="320" x="350" y="1172" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n7b" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=13;" value="&lt;b&gt;&#39;Resampling creates new data.&#39;&lt;/b&gt; It only reshuffles what you have. 1,000 resamples of 20 trades are still only 20 trades of evidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&#39;The bootstrap shows the worst case.&#39;&lt;/b&gt; It can&#39;t show a loss bigger than your journal&#39;s biggest, or a market you haven&#39;t traded.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&#39;Order doesn&#39;t matter.&#39;&lt;/b&gt; Simple resampling treats trades as independent. If losses cluster (same regime), real streaks and drawdowns can be worse." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="330" width="320" x="350" y="1204" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n8h" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;" value="8 · Minimal mathematics" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="32" width="320" x="680" y="1172" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n8b" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=13;" value="Data: x₁, …, xₙ (your n trades)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Repeat B times (for example B = 1,000):&lt;br&gt;• draw x*₁, …, x*ₙ from the data &lt;b&gt;with replacement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• compute the statistic θ̂* (average, drawdown, …)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;95% bootstrap interval&lt;/b&gt; = 2.5th to 97.5th percentile of the B values of θ̂*&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Bootstrap SE = SD of the θ̂* values. For the average it matches s ÷ √n (here ≈ 0.16R)." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="330" width="320" x="680" y="1204" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n9h" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;" value="9 · How to read the diagram above" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="32" width="320" x="1010" y="1172" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n9b" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B0B0B0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=13;" value="Left to right:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1 Observation:&lt;/b&gt; one journal, and questions (drawdown, streaks) with no formula.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2 Intuition:&lt;/b&gt; the journal becomes a bag; resample, score, repeat; pile up the averages.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3 Experiment:&lt;/b&gt; the drawdown pile, losing streaks, the chance of a losing 100 trades, and what risk per trade does to the bad case.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4 Insight:&lt;/b&gt; resample, score, pile; the blind spot; the takeaway." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="330" width="320" x="1010" y="1204" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n10h" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#2E7D32;strokeColor=#1B5E20;fontColor=#FFFFFF;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;" value="10 · Takeaway" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="32" width="320" x="1340" y="1172" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="b_n10b" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E8F5E9;strokeColor=#1B5E20;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=16;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1B5E20;" value="When there&#39;s no formula, reshuffle your own trades a thousand times and look at the pile." vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="330" width="320" x="1340" y="1204" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>